# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Measured on winoracle 2026-09-28 (Windows 11 10.0.26200, WARP "Microsoft
# Basic Render Driver"), run from an INTERACTIVE scheduled task
# (schtasks /it) -- from a plain ssh session (session 0) every window-bound
# DXGI call (MakeWindowAssociation, CreateSwapChain*) is
# DXGI_ERROR_NOT_CURRENTLY_AVAILABLE and nothing below is measurable:
#   schtasks /create /tn a11dxgi /tr "cmd /c C:\Users\owner\dxgi_a11_64.exe >
#     C:\Users\owner\a11dxgi64.txt 2>&1" /sc once /st 00:00 /f /it
#   schtasks /run /tn a11dxgi
# The logged-on session is DISCONNECTED, so every Present returns
# DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED (0x087a0001) and SetFullscreenState(TRUE) is
# DXGI_ERROR_NOT_CURRENTLY_AVAILABLE: only Present VALIDATION (which codes are
# INVALID_CALL) is measured here, not on-screen behaviour. The Basic Render
# Driver has NO outputs, so the [output] section is empty here and
# GetContainingOutput / GetFrameStatistics answer DXGI_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED;
# Vitreo's output rows are judged against Learn only.
# x86 differs from x64 only in CreateDXGIFactory2(DEBUG): SysWOW64 has
# DXGIDebug.dll, System32 does not -> x64 answers DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL.
#
# 2026-09-28 fix pass: every WRONG/MISSING row below except those listed
# under "Remaining" is fixed, and the probe no longer takes a "vitreo-safe"
# argument (run: vitreo run dxgi_a11_64.exe). Remaining differences: outputs
# (BRD has none), adapter identity, occluded-session Present/statistics,
# rows Windows crashes on, SetPrivateDataInterface (area 12), GDI surfaces
# (area 02), D3D10 CheckInterfaceSupport (frontend default-off), GetModule-
# Handle(dxgi.dll) (loader), DISCARD fmt=89 / samples=8 / 20000x20000 /
# stereo / studio colour space (Metal limits, UNIMPLEMENTED lines), buffer
# QI IDXGISurface, CreateSoftwareAdapter.
#
# Verdicts for Vitreo before the fix pass (then run with "vitreo-safe"). Full
# inventory: .docs/audits/2026-09-28-d3d11-contract-audit/area-11-dxgi.md.
#  HOST CRASHES (why "vitreo-safe" existed): CreateSwapChain with
#    R32G32B32A32_FLOAT or D24_UNORM_S8_UINT -> uncaught NSException
#    'CAMetalLayerInvalid' (Windows: E_INVALIDARG / DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL);
#    20000x20000 swap chain -> Metal texture-descriptor assertion (SIGABRT);
#    IDXGIOutput6::CheckHardwareCompositionSupport (vtable slot 28) is past the
#    end of the 28-entry output vtable -> guest jumps to 0 (0xC000001D).
#  WRONG: IID_IDXGIResource1 constant is wrong, so no object answers
#    IDXGIResource1 (CreateSharedHandle / CreateSubresourceSurface unreachable);
#    Present rejects SyncInterval 2..4 and every flag (TEST, DO_NOT_WAIT,
#    DO_NOT_SEQUENCE, RESTART, USE_DURATION, unknown bits) with INVALID_CALL;
#    CreateSwapChain* reject Width/Height 0 (Windows: window client size),
#    Windowed=FALSE (Windows: windowed chain + DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED) and MSAA
#    bitblt chains; ResizeBuffers(…0,0…) keeps the old size (Windows: client
#    size) and fails while the back buffer is only bound to the context;
#    no flip-model validation (count 1/17, sRGB, flags, usage, scaling, alpha);
#    GetBuffer refuses IDXGISurface/IDXGIResource/Texture2D1 and index>0 on
#    SEQUENTIAL; keyed-mutex state not shared across openings, no timeout
#    wait, E_FAIL instead of DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL, x86 truncates the key;
#    CreateDXGIFactory2 rejects flags 2/4/bit31; SetMaximumFrameLatency(0).
#  MISSING: IDXGISwapChain2/3/4, IDXGIDevice3/4, GetParent/ResizeTarget/
#    GetContainingOutput/GetFrameStatistics/background colour/rotation on the
#    swap chain, Register{Occlusion,Stereo}Status*, GetSharedResourceAdapter-
#    Luid, Offer/ReclaimResources, EnqueueSetEvent, GDI-compatible surfaces.
